  "notes": [
    "The numerical strip bound combines measured base-coordinate roundoff with a gamma4 arithmetic bound for texture-index conversion. It is not a global macro-expression roundoff proof.",
    "No slope smoothing, cell bias, or changed height sample is introduced.",
    "An actual renderer check must compare its operations to the same float32 oracle, then separately show exact-coordinate conditioning. A tiny global angle bound is mathematically impossible at native derivative jumps."
